    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Acyl groups can be built into many molecules using acyl chlorides or acid anhydrides (known as acylating agents). Acyl chlorides are **derivatives of carboxylic acids** by substitution of the -OH group by a chlorine atom. They are named by identifying the parent hydrocarbon chain and adding the suffix -*oyl chloride.* They can also be named by removing the -oic acid from the carboxylic acid and adding -*oyl chloride*",
    "reading_order" : 4,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000005",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Acid anhydrides are also **derivatives of carboxylic acids** formed by substitution of the -OH group by an alkanoate",
    "reading_order" : 5,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000006",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Acid anhydrides are named by identifying the parent hydrocarbon chain and adding the suffix -*oic anhydride*",
    "reading_order" : 6,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000007",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "They can also be named by removing the -oic acid from the carboxylic acid and adding -*oic anyhydride*",
    "reading_order" : 7,
